# WiseMind Execution Bot — Cursor operating rules

You are continuing the **WiseMind execution bot** for Michael (WiseMindFx): the Python service
(`bot.py`, `webhook_handler.py`, `mt5_executor.py`, `signal_utils.py`, `config.py`) that receives
TradingView alerts, scores them, and **auto-executes trades on MetaTrader 5 via MetaAPI**, plus the
breakeven monitor and the Telegram Claude coach. This work is shared with Claude Code via a "middle brain"
handoff file — treat that file as the source of truth.

> Sibling rule: `wisemind-ai.mdc` governs the **indicator** (`.pine`) work. THIS rule governs the
> **bot/execution** work. They share `~/AI Coding/CLAUDE.md` as the ecosystem map.

## ALWAYS read first (in this order)
1. `docs/BOT_HANDOFF.md` — bot status + full history + how-it-works + next-task queue + run/verify. **Start here.**
2. `~/AI Coding/CLAUDE.md` — full ecosystem map (bot + Core + Brain + HQ, rules, env vars).
3. `docs/HANDOFF.md` — the indicator brain (what the Pine scripts send to this bot).

## Hard rules (never break)
- **CONFIRM BEFORE CHANGES.** Michael's standing rule: *"always confirm with me so you understand"* and
  *"be precise, don't make mistakes — this is my life work."* Plan → get a yes → then edit.
- **NEVER auto-trade without an explicit go.** Default `.env` is safe: `MT5_EXECUTION_ENABLED=false` +
  `MT5_DRY_RUN=true`. Only flip to live when Michael says so. Leave it safe when you finish.
- **Demo first.** Prove execution changes on the IC Markets demo (open → observe → close) before real
  money. On real money start `MT5_MIN_GRADE=A+` and confirm `ACCOUNT_BALANCE` matches.
- **Pine is the brain; the bot is the hand.** Execute the alert's exact entry/SL/TP. The bot only adds lot
  size, the grade filter, and breakeven management. Never re-derive entry/SL/TP.
- **Secrets via `.env` only.** Never hardcode the MetaAPI token / Telegram token / Claude key; never
  commit `.env`.
- **Verify before "done."** Syntax-check Python; prove execution changes on demo. No "this should work."
- **DOCUMENT EVERYTHING, ALWAYS (standing order).** Proactively keep `docs/BOT_HANDOFF.md` fully current
  every session — history, current work, AND all future/roadmap/vision (short-term, long-term, product/
  sell ideas, even half-formed ones). Michael should never have to ask. If it isn't in the handoff, it
  didn't happen. This is how you and Claude Code stay on the same page.

## Workflow
- Pick the **top item of `docs/BOT_HANDOFF.md` §5** unless told otherwise; propose the plan first.
- Run/verify per BOT_HANDOFF §2: start the bot, `curl` a test signal at `/webhook`, confirm the Telegram +
  execution result, and (for execution changes) open/close a position on demo to prove it.
- **When you finish a slice, update the handoff** per BOT_HANDOFF §6: move the item into §3 with
  file/function/param detail + how it was verified, update §4 if capabilities changed, re-order §5, add any
  new `.env` keys, and leave `.env` safe + the demo account flat.

## Style
- Precision over speed; this moves real orders. Preserve the domain depth (T1/T2 AMD, sessions, sweeps,
  FVG/OB, grades, smart SL/TP). Comment the *why*. Surface trade-offs. Only edit after Michael confirms.
- Known gotchas (already fixed — don't reintroduce): MetaAPI rejects a `clientId` and a `+`/symbols in the
  order comment; `metaapi-cloud-sdk` needs `anthropic>=0.105` + `httpx>=0.28` (don't re-pin httpx to 0.27).
